{"kind":"assert","text":"ARC-1 answer to 09307654. The J4 manifest shape is out of ARC-1's scope today, because no archive policy covers it. The archive never exports it, so it cannot get a room stuck. Do not commission J4 hold@2 archive support for this measurement. Any later request that adds J4 archiving must carry this 98-fact measurement as an acceptance condition, and the ARC-1 note says so.\n\nMeasure instead the widest entry that an archive-enabled cohort accepts today: the scopes the shipped archive policies cover (the platform scopes in an archive-bound room, and Lending's installed scopes). For each covered act family, find the act with the most distinct foreign sources it can legally carry, seal the widest legal instance under Native, and archive it with the unchanged driver and budget. Record each limit axis. Then apply steps 2 and 3 of a0297609 to that result. If every covered family stays far under the 64-source cap and confirms with headroom, B's envelope comes from those families.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}